<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3152-LOCALIPCWAKE-NONHTTP-TRAFFIC>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3152-LOCALIPCWAKE-NONHTTP-TRAFFIC" ;
  triage:title "local_ipc_wake.rs is non-HTTP-framed traffic, violates Phase AI HTTP-over-UDS design goal" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr's M5-ADMISSION-POSTMERGE-REVIEWERBACKED review (task #1417, PASS on the 6 originally-tracked M5 findings) surfaced this as a NEW, out-of-scope finding on integrate/phase-ai-31-33 @ c9ba04d9: crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_wake.rs is the sole non-HTTP-framed traffic in the entire transport stack — a raw connect+flush wake-poke used to unblock a blocked accept() call during shutdown. This violates Phase AI's HTTP-over-UDS design goal (docs/project-plan.md:970, which mandates all local IPC traffic be HTTP-framed). The user has directed that non-HTTP traffic be flagged for deletion on code-cleanliness grounds. However, quality-mgr flags that deleting it needs a real replacement accept()-unblock mechanism (e.g. non-blocking accept() with a poll/select loop, or calling shutdown(2) on the listening file descriptor to force accept() to return) — a bare removal without a replacement would regress the bounded-shutdown-join fix (the 6 just-fixed M5 findings) back into a hang, because shutdown would have no way to unblock a thread parked in accept()." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "architecture" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S13 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-03T00:10:11Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3152-LOCALIPCWAKE-NONHTTP-TRAFFIC/integrate-phase-ai-31-33-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-03T01:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:progressNote "AI3152-LOCALIPCWAKE-QA-1 (fix/localipcwake-accept-interrupt @ f12eb72e, PR #725): fixed. local_ipc_wake.rs deleted entirely; local UDS and Unix loopback TCP (both unix and windows cfg arms) listeners now use nonblocking accept() polled at a 1ms interval, checking shutdown_beacon/lifecycle terminate each iteration -- no dummy self-connect remains. req-qa (closed, independent workspace grep), arch-qa (closed, confirms no non-HTTP-framed traffic on any transport socket, bounded shutdown latency preserved), ruthless-boundary-qa (FIXED, scope-locked), rust-qa-agent (PASS, fmt/clippy/tests green, no remaining wake call sites), rust-service-hardening-agent (PASS, shutdown chain independently traced end-to-end as bounded) all independently corroborate. This QA round's overall verdict is FAIL for unrelated reasons (arch-qa found a new RULE-003 file-size blocker on local_ipc_transport.rs, and req-qa flagged the cited unit test as not actually proving the shutdown-interrupt claim) -- neither blocks closure of this specific finding, which is resolved on the reviewed commit." .

